// Capture 3.4 review candidate: auto settings, readback gate, death ledgers, E33, per-player friendly and GrowthP2.
// CM balance telemetry (v3 encoding; capture schema 3.4).
// Records 5-second, per-unit-type combat telemetry to two dedicated local banks.
// Recording is opt-in (manual command or saved auto preference). Capture triggers remain disabled, except match-local birth/revive evidence;
// nothing samples until a player types "-baltrace on".
//
// v3.2 vs 3.1a (purely additive; MeasureVersion stays 3.1 — no existing column changes what
// it counts):
//   * Growth vector widened 9 -> 11: G10 = MalashBreak casts (hero ultimate "tear reality"),
//     G11 = MalashImmortalOrder casts (walker "immortal order" mark).
//   * Samples slots carry a 6th field "a" = attack instances that reached the damage handler,
//     counted BEFORE the amount gate, so fully-absorbed hits still count. Splash onto several
//     targets in one attack is deduplicated per slot by (source unit, effect, mission time).
//   * bank 2 gains a 5th stream "Field": t|hu,hs,nu,ns = hostile-to-P1 on-field life+shields
//     (int-truncated), split non-structure / structure, with matching unit counts. One
//     full-map enumeration per sample.
//
// v3 vs v2
//   * Own accumulators (CMBT_Acc / CMBT_AccInt / CMBT_EnemyAcc) instead of reading UT_DL.
//     UT_DL's slot table is shared with the player-facing "-dl" panel and can be cleared
//     mid-game, which corrupted v2's delta baseline. v3 owns its slots end to end and only
//     reuses UT_DL's "linear search by unit type, merge morph pairs" idea.
//   * Two banks (same epoch suffix, same frame numbers):
//       bank 1 "CMCombatTelemetry<epoch>"  : Meta / Units / Samples
//                Samples frame = t|P1(slot:d/n/h/o/dn/a,..)|P2(..)
//       bank 2 "CMCombatTelemetryX<epoch>" : Meta / Units / Taken / Enemy / Growth / Field
//                Taken  frame = t|P1(slot:tl/ts/de/ds/hl/hs,..)|P2(..)
//                Enemy  frame = t|e:d,..            (enemy unit type -> damage onto P1+P2)
//                Growth frame = t|g1,..,g11         (commander-specific integer vector; Malash
//                                                    wired: attributes / obedience / cast counts,
//                                                    empty token = not observable this frame)
//                Field  frame = t|hu,hs,nu,ns       (hostile-to-P1 on-field life+shields and
//                                                    unit counts, non-structure / structure)
//   * Each section packs CMBT_FRAMES_PER_CHUNK frames per key "C<n>"; every section stays
//     under CMBT_MAX_CHUNKS keys (720 samples / 6 = 120 <= 128) and the cap is asserted.
//   * Both banks are saved every sample, so a crash loses at most the last 5 seconds.
//
// The two CMBT_UT_DL_* helpers below are called from LibCOTF's damage-logging trigger
// (Nova's source-less air strike credit). They are part of UT_DL, not of the telemetry
// capture path, and are kept byte-for-byte compatible with v2.

const string CMBT_SCRIPT_VERSION = "v3";
// Measurement semantics version. Bumped when what a column *counts* changes, even if the
// encoding does not. 3.1 = T0/T7/T8 count only damage whose victim is hostile to the source.
const string CMBT_MEASURE_VERSION = "3.1";
// Capture 3.1a observes unknown alliances; neutral classification remains pending.
// d/hits/overkill retain their hostile-victim meaning; dn is reserved and stays zero.
// 3.2 adds columns only: G10/G11 cast counts, the Samples "a" attack-instance field and the
// bank 2 "Field" stream. No existing column changes what it counts.
const string CMBT_CAPTURE_SCHEMA = "3.4";
